<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n23472" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ĭnĭmīco</span></b> ,
		1, v. a.
		inimicus, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>to make enemies</i>, <i>to set at
				variance</i> (<b>poet.</b> and rare): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">miseras inimicat urbes,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Hor.
					C. 4, 15, 20</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">hostiles inimicant classica turmas,</span>”
				<i>urge on to fight</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Stat.
					Th. 2, 419</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pectora,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Aus. Ep. 24, 63</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Sid. Ep. 5, 19</span></i>.—<b>
				<i>Absol.</i>
			</b>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">desine inimicari,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Eccli. 28, 6</span></i>
			.</div>
